{"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"text":"Run a synthetic feed through the example and review every row’s disposition.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"title":"Inspecting normalization decisions","role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"FitnessEventDataPipeline"}]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Run the supplied fixture","type":"heading","anchor":"Run-the-supplied-fixture","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"From the repository root, use Swift 6.0 or later:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"sh","code":["swift run normalize-events < Fixtures\/synthetic-events.json"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The checked fixture produces one normalized event and five receipts. Compare the JSON semantically with ","type":"text"},{"code":"Fixtures\/expected-output.json","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; whitespace and object-key order are not part of the contract. The executable also returns a nonzero exit status for malformed input JSON.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"These are local teaching-package checks. The manifest declares macOS 13 and iOS 16 minimums, but current execution evidence is on macOS. It does not establish an iPhone-device run or a released ShowFlex data pipeline.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Inspect events and receipts separately","type":"heading","anchor":"Inspect-events-and-receipts-separately","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"code":"events","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" array contains accepted ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ac.robin.educational.fitness-event-data-pipeline\/documentation\/FitnessEventDataPipeline\/NormalizedEvent","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" values sorted by stable identity. The ","type":"text"},{"code":"receipts","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" array contains one ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ac.robin.educational.fitness-event-data-pipeline\/documentation\/FitnessEventDataPipeline\/Receipt","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" per original input row, preserving the input index so a caller can explain omissions as well as successful output.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Decision"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Meaning"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"accepted"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A valid, unique normalized payload remains in the accepted output."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"duplicate"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An equivalent normalized payload repeats the same source\/external identity."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rejected"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The row fails validation; it does not enter the accepted output."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"conflict"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Valid rows disagree for the same identity; every related valid row is quarantined.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"header":"row"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Conflict handling can revise an earlier receipt from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"accepted"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"duplicate"},{"type":"text","text":" to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"conflict"},{"type":"text","text":". Inspect the final report rather than treating an intermediate decision as permanent. Input order never chooses a winner for conflicting valid payloads."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Review the policy boundaries","anchor":"Review-the-policy-boundaries"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ac.robin.educational.fitness-event-data-pipeline\/documentation\/FitnessEventDataPipeline\/RawEvent","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" supplies explicit timestamps and an HTTPS source URL. Source slugs are trimmed and lowercased; external identifiers remain case-sensitive. The accepted event ID joins them with a colon. Title normalization collapses whitespace; it does not merge unrelated events by title."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Dates require seconds and an explicit UTC offset. Output uses UTC. A missing end timestamp remains unknown. Unsupported date-only, fractional-second or recurrence forms need a separate policy and are outside this example.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A retained source URL is a provenance pointer. It is not independent corroboration of the event’s truth. URLs containing embedded credentials or fragments are rejected; the package makes no request to them.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","text":"Apply the library contract","anchor":"Apply-the-library-contract","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Consumers call ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ac.robin.educational.fitness-event-data-pipeline\/documentation\/FitnessEventDataPipeline\/EventNormalizer\/normalize(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" with an array of ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ac.robin.educational.fitness-event-data-pipeline\/documentation\/FitnessEventDataPipeline\/RawEvent","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" values and receive a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ac.robin.educational.fitness-event-data-pipeline\/documentation\/FitnessEventDataPipeline\/NormalizationReport","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". There is no persistence layer, authenticated provider integration or retry scheduler. Those decisions belong to a real ingestion service and require their own evidence and tests."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants